  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through Sunday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: The area will be under a dry southwest \nflow aloft today through Wednesday. Conditions will generally be \ndry, with light winds except for Central Nevada. Winds across White \nPine County will be out of the southwest near 20 mph, with gusts \nnear 35 mph each afternoon. Highs will be in the 70s for Tuesday and \nwarming into the 70s and 80s Wednesday afternoon. Overnight lows \nwill be in the 30s and 40s.\n\nBy Thursday and Friday, all models are depicting an upper level \ntrough diving to the south. This will bring breezy afternoon winds \nwith highs in the 70s and 80s. At this time, the airmass is \nanticipated to remain on the dry side. Overnight lows will be in the \n30s.\n\nOn Saturday and Sunday, expect continued dry conditions, with highs \nin the 70s and 80s and lows in the 30s and 40s.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: No changes were made to the NBM \nforecast. Confidence is high regarding unseasonably cool \ntemperatures today. Moderate to high confidence exists Wednesday and \nThursday as temperatures gradually warm, climbing to at or just \nabove normal conditions.",
